## Reading measured differences honestly

- `damage_committed` total includes damage inflicted on enemies. Partition actual events by target==player, enemy and environment damage_kind before talking about harm/fairness.
- Only compare duration/interaction for appropriately completed goals or common observed intervals; early failed/shorter trace is not an improvement. More interactions can also just mean farther coverage, not content quality.
- Compare initial capability and record actual selected reward type/final build. Policy prefers ResourceRewardChoice; do not infer constant runtime build solely from initial_capability.
- Legacy blind80 vs aware new80 is not a content comparison. Actual new aware old80/new80 is primary. Four-smoke observations remain intermediate and no general human success-rate.
- Root final Foundry repeat changes resources/foundry generated outputs: register a real development-only level_module recertification record before quality profiles, formal_impact=false, no new formal pool. Preserve old v9 record/evidence.


