## Necessary final analysis fix under root main scope, only after active leases terminal

Current level_experience.report worst_candidates sorts total damage_committed, mixing damage to enemies/bells with damage to player. Do not present this as player hurt/fairness. Prefer a small explicit analysis_version=2 (threshold POLICY unchanged), ranking actual target==player damage rather than damage dealt. Include numeric player/non_player/unknown damage counts, never a fun score. report(...,analysis_version=1) must return byte-semantic original structure without the new member/stats and original sort; validate_report dispatches saved report.get(analysis_version,1), keeping original archived v1 fingerprints exactly recomputable. New default reports carry analysis_version2; compare must explicitly reject algorithm-version mismatch and unknown/bool versions. This is one existing analyzer contract/version, no new checker. Meaningful tests: nonplayer damage does not outrank true player harm; saved legacyv1 recomputation and v1/v2 mismatch rejection. Check actual downstream original-v2 fingerprint consumers use saved algorithm version where required, no archived rewrites. No new checker/framework; existing level-experience check. Same final before/after reports must both use identical new policy. If no fix executed, explicitly retain biased legacy worst list as candidate only and select trueplayer-damage worst with source evidence in final audit; never claim sorted total damage is player harm. This is a concrete audit defect, not permission to grow tools indefinitely.


